intro
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:09.800
How Tribu turns a study into insights
The agent swarm, step by step

s00-a
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.000
// 00 · DATA
It starts with raw survey data.

s00-b
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Code — not judgment — cleans it,
so every number can be re-run.

s00-c
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.800
Raw CSV → clean base, codebook, tables.
Duplicates and inconsistencies removed.

s01-a
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.000
// 01 · ARCHITECT
An architect agent builds the team.

s01-b
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.000
It reads the client's questions and decides
who runs, and with which techniques.

s01-c
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:35.800
Analysis · control · story · quality:
140 agents, sized to the study.

s02-a
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.000
// 02 · ANALYSIS
Every key question is attacked several ways.

s02-b
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:45.500
Analysts work in parallel, blind to each other,
each with a different technique.

s02-c
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:52.000
Explainable ML, choice model, segmentation,
text analytics — plus techniques found by a scout.

cur-a
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:56.500
// THE CURRENCY
Agents exchange only one thing: the finding card.

cur-b
00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:00.500
No prose travels between agents.
Every result must arrive in this form.

cur-c
00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:05.000
Claim · base · test · script.
One card = one finding, traceable to its data.

s03-a
00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:09.500
// 03 · ARBITER
An arbiter weighs the techniques against each other.

s03-b
00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:13.500
The method that explains most with the data
available wins — not the fanciest one.

s03-c
00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.300
They agree → strong finding.
They disagree → the gap is the insight.

s03-d
00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:19.000
Only one sees it → kept with a caveat.

ver-a
00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:23.500
// 03 · VERIFY
Independent agents recompute every number.

ver-b
00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:28.000
They never saw the analysis. A devil's advocate
tests the alternative explanation.

ver-c
00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.500
Verified · Verified · Rejected.
Only verified cards can be cited by a slide.

s04-a
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:37.000
// 04 · STORY
Then the story — with four human approvals.

s04-b
00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:41.500
Tribu's strategists sign off at each step
before the deck exists.

s04-c
00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:47.000
1 Conclusion · 2 Slide flow · 3 Design + charts
4 Full deck — headline = the finding.

why-a
00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:52.500
// WHY IT MATTERS
Up to 140 agents. Several techniques per question.

why-b
00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:58.800
Every number traceable.
Deeper insights — and the judgment stays human.

end
00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:07.000
tribu
Next generation market research
